<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<adaptive-icon xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android">
    <!--
        Two layers, so the launcher's own shape is filled edge to edge.

        The background is the Senyera, and it is laid to be seen: all nine bands
        — five gold and the four red bars — fall inside the middle 72dp, which
        is the most of this canvas any launcher shows. Laid across the whole
        108dp instead, as it was at first, every mask cut it down to three bars
        and left something that was merely striped red and gold rather than the
        flag. The pattern carries on past the edge of what is shown until the
        canvas is covered, so whatever shape is cut — Samsung's squircle, a
        Pixel's circle — it is cut out of flag, with no ground at the corners.
        The satin light along each band is the artwork's own.

        The foreground is the open book and its rose, standing 48dp wide in the
        middle: whole through a circle, with the flag readable either side of it
        rather than a finger's width of stripe. A soft shadow of its own sits
        under it, because the one painted into the artwork fell on stripes that
        are not in this layer any more.

        Both layers are built from tools/icon/artwork.png by tools/icon/build.py
        rather than cut by hand, so the next time the artwork changes this is one
        command and not an afternoon.
    -->
    <background android:drawable="@mipmap/ic_launcher_background" />
    <foreground android:drawable="@mipmap/ic_launcher_foreground" />
    <monochrome android:drawable="@drawable/ic_launcher_monochrome" />
</adaptive-icon>
